## Deliberately not shipped

**Chicago font files.** The display role names Chicago, as the ChicagoFLF
revival. No binary is in this repository or in its history: the `@font-face`
rule resolves it with `local()` only, so a machine that already has Chicago uses
it and every other machine renders the display role in Archivo. That is what the
published site renders in today. Shipping Chicago means either clearing the
redistribution terms of a revival or drawing the display type as outlines;
`scripts/check_assets.py` refuses every font binary until that is settled.

**Macintosh icon set.** The design language no longer calls for one. Susan
Kare's 1984 Macintosh icons seeded the earlier Sys7 direction; those icons are
Apple's and none of them are in this repository or in its history. The current
system marks things with type and hairlines rather than icons, so nothing is
pending.

The rule this repository follows: assets whose provenance is not clean never
enter the history, because git history is permanent and deleting a file later
does not remove it.
